CHAPTER VI
INSTITUTIONAL ARRANGEMENTS
Article 11
(1) In the case of providing protection to women and children victims of violence, the regional government may establish an Integrated Service Center (PPT).
jdih.pakpakbharatkab.go.id - 8 - (2) The establishment and development of PPT shall be adjusted to the development of priority needs, regional financial capacity, and the institutional capacity of personnel available in the region.
(3) The PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) may accommodate institutions/work units that provide services for victims of violence such as P2TP2A, Safe Houses, Child Social Protection Houses, Trauma Center Houses, Women's Social Protection Houses, Shelters and other service activities in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.
(4) Forms of services implemented by PPT include:
a. complaints;
b. health rehabilitation;
c. social rehabilitation;
d. legal assistance;
e. repatriation;
f. social reintegration.
(5) In providing protection to women and children victims of violence, PPT is obligated to:
a. provide services as quickly as possible and free of charge to victims; b. organize protection and fulfillment of victims' rights to health rehabilitation, social rehabilitation, repatriation, social reintegration and legal assistance;
c. cooperate with certain institutions in providing translators and volunteer assistants needed for victims; d. network with government or private hospitals for treatment and health recovery of victims and cooperate with witness and victim protection institutions, social protection houses or trauma centers owned by the government, community or other institutions for victims' health recovery;
e. provide convenience, comfort, and safety for victims; f. maintain confidentiality of victims;
g. provide fulfillment of legal assistance for victims;
h. in the case that integrated service provision is carried out through networking, PPT remains responsible for the entire referral process of services needed by victims.
(6) The provision of integrated services as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be implemented in accordance with SPM.

Article 13
SPM as referred to in Article 12 has performance indicators including:
a. coverage of women and children victims of violence who receive complaint handling, health services, social rehabilitation services, spiritual guidance services conducted by trained officers within integrated service units;
b. coverage of law enforcement from the investigation level up to court decisions on cases of violence against women and children;
c. coverage of women and children victims of violence who receive legal aid services;
d. coverage of repatriation services for women and children victims of violence; and
e. coverage of social reintegration services for women and children victims of violence.

Article 7
(1) The obligations and responsibilities of the community as referred to in Article 5 letter b, shall be implemented in the form of community participation. (2) The form of community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), includes:
a. preventing the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children;
b. providing information and/or reporting acts of violence against women and children to law enforcement or the competent authorities;
c. participating in the handling of victims of acts of violence;
d. providing protection to victims; and
e. providing emergency assistance.
